    <item>
      <title>Go Daily Question 20250510</title>
      <link>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_20250510/</link>
      <pubDate>Sat, 10 May 2025 00:27:26 +0800</pubDate>
      <guid>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_20250510/</guid>
      <category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/godailyquestion/">GoDailyQuestion</category>
      <category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/golanguagebasics/">GoLanguageBasics</category>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Will the following code run normally, and what is the result?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;package main&#xA;&#xA;func main() {&#xA;    v := new(int)&#xA;    *v = 2&#xA;    println(5/&amp;#43;-*v)&#xA;}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&lt;details&gt;&#xA;  &lt;summary&gt;🔑 Answer Analysis:&lt;/summary&gt;&#xA;  &lt;p&gt;It runs normally and the result is -2.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://go.dev/play/p/5A8BdXFzaOf&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;external nofollow noopener noreferrer&#34;&gt;Run online&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 class=&#34;heading-element&#34; id=&#34;expression-parsing&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;Expression Parsing&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;  &lt;a href=&#34;#expression-parsing&#34; class=&#34;heading-mark&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;svg class=&#34;octicon octicon-link&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 16 16&#34; version=&#34;1.1&#34; width=&#34;16&#34; height=&#34;16&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34;&gt;&lt;path d=&#34;m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z&#34;&gt;&lt;/path&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;5/+-*v&lt;/code&gt;&#xA;Go language &lt;a href=&#34;https://golang.google.cn/ref/spec#Operators&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;external nofollow noopener noreferrer&#34;&gt;operator precedence rules&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Go Daily Question 222</title>
      <link>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_222/</link>
      <pubDate>Sat, 03 May 2025 00:37:04 +0800</pubDate>
      <guid>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_222/</guid>
      <category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/godailyquestion/">GoDailyQuestion</category>
      <category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/golanguagebasics/">GoLanguageBasics</category>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Go101 author published a twitter. Will the following code run normally, and what is the result?&#xA;What is the output of the following code?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;package main&#xA;&#xA;func main() {&#xA;    v := new(int)&#xA;    *v = 2&#xA;    println(5/&amp;#43;-*v)&#xA;}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&lt;details&gt;&#xA;  &lt;summary&gt;🔑 Answer Analysis:&lt;/summary&gt;&#xA;  &lt;p&gt;Reference Answer and Analysis: B.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Go has the following unary operators:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;unary_op = &amp;#34;&amp;#43;&amp;#34; | &amp;#34;-&amp;#34; | &amp;#34;!&amp;#34; | &amp;#34;^&amp;#34; | &amp;#34;*&amp;#34; | &amp;#34;&amp;amp;&amp;#34; | &amp;#34;&amp;lt;-&amp;#34; .&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;p&gt;Therefore, &lt;code&gt;5/+-*v&lt;/code&gt; will be calculated first.&#xA;Also, according to the specification:&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Go Daily Question 209</title>
      <link>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_209/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 10 Mar 2025 11:03:42 +0800</pubDate>
      <guid>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_209/</guid>
      <category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/godailyquestion/">GoDailyQuestion</category>
      <category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/golanguagebasics/">GoLanguageBasics</category>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;What is the output of the following code?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;package main&#xA;&#xA;import &amp;#34;fmt&amp;#34;&#xA;&#xA;func main() {&#xA;    var a, b float64 = 1.0, 4.0&#xA;    fmt.Println(a | b)&#xA;}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;p&gt;A: 5&#xA;B: +Inf&#xA;C: panic&#xA;D: Cannot compile&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;details&gt;&#xA;  &lt;summary&gt;🔑 Answer Analysis:&lt;/summary&gt;&#xA;  &lt;p&gt;D Cannot compile&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://go.dev/play/p/lLMbGE_ajrg&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;external nofollow noopener noreferrer&#34;&gt;Run online&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The &lt;code&gt;|&lt;/code&gt; operator is a bitwise OR operator, and its operands can only be integers. In the problem above, the operands are &lt;code&gt;float64&lt;/code&gt;, so it will not compile.&#xA;Compilation error message:&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
